# Environment boundary

- Default host instructions to Windows PowerShell 7 and label them clearly.
- Use Git Bash only for explicitly labeled Bash/POSIX-compatible local work.
- The real Sprite runtime is Linux/Bash with case-sensitive paths and no
  Windows drive letters, `.cmd` executables, or PowerShell assumption.
- Use UTF-8 without BOM and LF for shared source and every runtime file.
- Use CRLF only for Windows-only `.ps1`, `.cmd`, and `.bat` entrypoints.
- Prefer portable TypeScript/Python path and process APIs over shell glue.
- Verify runtime behavior in Linux CI and, when authorized, a disposable Sprite.
